---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Market Analysis — Desk Support Monkey" description="Spain-first strategy, EU market sizing, NIS2 compliance wave timeline. 35,000–45,000 Spanish SMBs facing NIS2 pressure.">
  <div class="pt-24 pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">

      <a href="/transparency" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-700 transition-colors mb-6">
        <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Transparency
      </a>

      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-3">Market Analysis</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: February 2026 · Focus: Spain (months 1–6) → Europe (year 2+)</p>

      <!-- Key insight -->
      <div class="mb-10 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900 p-6 text-white">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">The real competitor is Excel</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          67% of EU SMBs still manage IT assets in spreadsheets or manually. Only 12% have a mature IT management framework.
          The primary competitor is not Freshservice or Lansweeper — it is a shared Google Sheet with a list of laptops.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The sales conversation is not "why switch from competitor X" — it is "why stop using a spreadsheet."
          NIS2 answers that question better than any feature comparison.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Spain Phase 1 -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Phase 1 — Spain (Months 1–6)</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 mb-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-600">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Segment</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-semibold">Companies</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-700">
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">SMBs with 10–249 employees</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right">~180,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">NIS2-affected companies (all sizes)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right">~25,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">NIS2-affected SMBs (50–249 emp.) in direct scope</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right">~12,000–15,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Small enterprises (10–49 emp.) with indirect NIS2 supply chain pressure</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right">~20,000–30,000</td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-blue-50"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-blue-900">Total addressable in Spain (10–300 emp., NIS2 pressure)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-bold text-blue-900">~35,000–45,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">Of those: currently using spreadsheets (67%)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right text-slate-500">~23,000–30,000</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-2 mt-5">Why Spain first</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
          {[
            'Home market — no translation needed, no cultural barrier',
            "Founder's professional network is in Spain",
            'Spanish SMBs heavily represented in NIS2 Annex sectors: food, manufacturing, logistics, health',
            'Relatively low ITAM software penetration vs. Germany or Netherlands',
            '100% online sales — no geographic constraint within Spain',
          ].map((item) => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <svg class="mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-blue-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              {item}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- EU expansion -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Phase 2 — Europe (Year 2+)</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 mb-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-600">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Country</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">NIS2-affected companies</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Priority</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-700">
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Germany</td><td class="px-4 py-3">30,000–40,000</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-red-600 bg-red-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">High</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Italy</td><td class="px-4 py-3">27,000–50,000</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-red-600 bg-red-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">High</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="bg-blue-50"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-blue-900">Spain</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-blue-700">~25,000</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-blue-700 bg-blue-100 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Phase 1</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">France</td><td class="px-4 py-3">&gt;10,000</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-amber-700 bg-amber-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Medium</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Netherlands</td><td class="px-4 py-3">~8,000</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="text-xs font-medium text-amber-700 bg-amber-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">Medium</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600"><strong>Expansion sequence:</strong> Spain → Germany + Italy → France → Netherlands</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Compliance wave timeline -->
      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">The Compliance Wave Timeline</h2>
        <div class="relative border-l-2 border-blue-200 pl-6 space-y-5">
          {[
            { date: 'Oct 2024', event: 'NIS2 enforceable. Companies start receiving letters.' },
            { date: 'Jan 2025', event: 'DORA active. Financial sector scrambling.' },
            { date: 'Mar 2026', event: 'Desk Support Monkey launches.', highlight: true },
            { date: 'Sep 2026', event: 'First audit cycles. Companies realize they need documentation now.' },
            { date: 'Sep 2027', event: 'CRA reporting obligations begin.' },
            { date: 'Dec 2027', event: 'Full compliance boom. NIS2 + DORA + CRA all active simultaneously.' },
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="relative">
              <div class:list={[
                'absolute -left-7.5 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2',
                item.highlight ? 'border-blue-600 bg-blue-600' : 'border-blue-300 bg-white'
              ]}></div>
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class:list={[
                  'shrink-0 text-xs font-semibold',
                  item.highlight ? 'text-blue-600' : 'text-slate-500'
                ]}>{item.date}</span>
                <span class:list={[
                  'text-sm',
                  item.highlight ? 'font-medium text-slate-900' : 'text-slate-600'
                ]}>{item.event}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-slate-600 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
          The product launches 18 months before peak demand. Early enough to build community and trust,
          late enough that the regulation is real and companies feel the pressure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Key insight -->
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-green-200 bg-green-50 p-5 text-sm">
        <p class="font-semibold text-green-900 mb-1">The math is not ambitious — it is conservative</p>
        <p class="text-green-800 leading-relaxed">
          Reaching €300K ARR requires only 126–252 paying customers depending on plan mix.
          In a market of 35,000–45,000 Spanish SMBs alone facing NIS2 pressure, that is a 0.3–0.7% market share.
          The bottleneck is not market size — it is awareness.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
